hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17297","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Ali ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Ash'ari, he said: A man of them was killed at Awtas, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Abu Amir, why did you not change? Then he recited this verse: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves, he who strays harms you not when you are guided, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry and said: Where have you gone? It is only: O you who believe, he who strays of the disbelievers harms you not when you are guided."
"17298","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Maladh narrating from Numayr ibn Aws, from Malik ibn Masruh, from Amir ibn Abi Amir al-Ash'ari, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: What excellent tribe are al-Asd and al-Ash'ariyyun, they do not flee in battle nor misappropriate, they are of me and I am of them, Amir said: So I narrated it to Mu'awiya, so he said: Not thus did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, but he said: They are of me and to me, so he said: Not thus did my father narrate to me from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but he said: They are of me and I am of them, he said: Then you are more knowledgeable of the hadith of your father, Abd Allah said: This is of the best hadith, none narrated it but Jarir."
"17299","Abu al-Yaman informed us, Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Amir or Abu Amir or Abu Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting in a gathering with his companions, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him in other than his form, thinking him a man of the Muslims, and greeted him, so he returned the greeting, then Jibril placed his hand on the knees of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? So he said: That you submit your face to Allah, and testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and establish prayer and give zakat, he said: Then if I do that I have submitted? He said: Yes, then he said: What is faith? He said: That you believe in Allah and the Last Day and the angels and the Book and the prophets and death and life after death and Paradise and Hell and the reckoning and the balance and decree, all of it, its good and its evil, he said: Then if I do that I have believed? He said: Yes, then he said: What is excellence, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That you worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him He sees you, he said: Then if I do that I have excelled? He said: Yes, and we hear the return of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to him, while the one speaking to him is not seen nor his speech heard, he said: Then when is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Glory be to Allah, five of the unseen none knows but Allah Almighty: Allah has with Him knowledge of the Hour, and sends down rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die, indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware, so the questioner said: O Messenger of Allah, if you wish I will tell you two signs before it, so he said: Tell me, so he said: When you see the slavegirl begetting her master, and the builders prolonging with building, and the destitute barefoot returning as heads of people, he said: And who are those, O Messenger of Allah? He said: al-Arib, he said: Then he turned away, and when we no longer saw his path, he said: Glory be to Allah, three times, this is Jibril come to teach people their religion, and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, he never came to me but that I knew him, except this time."
"17300","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade kinds of women, and mentioned the hadith."
"17301","And he mentioned, attached to it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a sitting, then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the hadith, and he said in it: If you wish, I will tell you of signs thereof short of that. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, tell me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the slave woman give birth to her mistress, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17640","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, who said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Maladh, from Numayr ibn Aws, from Malik ibn Masruh, from 'Amir ibn Abi 'Amir al-Ash'ari, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What an excellent clan are al-Asad and al-Ash'ariyyun; they do not flee in battle nor misappropriate; they are from me and I am from them. 'Amir said: I narrated it to Mu'awiyah, and he said: This is not how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it; he only said: They are from me and toward me. I said: My father did not narrate it to me like this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he said: They are from me and I am from them. He said: Then you know the hadith of your father best."
"17641","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shu'ayb informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, who said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from 'Amir, or Abu 'Amir, or Abu Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was sitting in a gathering among his companions, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him in other than his form, supposed to be a man from the Muslims. He greeted him, and he returned the greeting. Then Jibril placed his hand upon the knees of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He said: That you submit your face to Allah, testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establish prayer, and give zakat. He said: If I do that, then I have submitted? He said: Yes. Then he said: What is faith? He said: That you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, the prophets, death, life after death, Paradise, Fire, reckoning, the balance, and decree, all of it, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that, then I have believed? He said: Yes. Then he said: What is excellence, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That you worship Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, then I have done excellently? He said: Yes. And the echo of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answering him could be heard, while the one speaking to him could not be seen nor his speech heard. He said: When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, five matters of the unseen which none knows but Allah: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, He sends down rain, knows what is in the wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware. The questioner said: O Messenger of Allah, if you wish I can tell you of two signs that will be before it. He said: Tell me. He said: When you see the slave woman giving birth to her master, and the builders of buildings competing in height, and the barefoot, dry, destitute become the heads of people. He said: And who are those, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Arabs. He said: Then he turned away and his path was not seen after. He said: Glory be to Allah, three times. He came to teach people their religion. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, he never came to me but I recognized him, except that this time might be it."
"17642","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade categories of women, and he mentioned the hadith."
"17643","Attached to it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a gathering, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. And he said in it: If you wish, I can tell you of signs of it short of that. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, tell me. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the slave woman giving birth to her mistress, and he mentioned the hadith."
